<title>GERMANY: Hoechst considering generics investments.</title>
<headline>Hoechst considering generics investments.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday it was analysing various options for its generics businesses Rugby, Copley and Cox after losses at the firm last year.</p>
<p>In its annual report Hoechst AG said that its Copley generic drugs group posted a loss of 19 million marks last year after high structural costs and compensation costs.</p>
<p>Hoechst also said that a strong drop in prices could not be offset by higher volume sales and new products last year. Generic drugs are cheaper versions of drugs whose patent protection has lapsed.</p>
<p>Hoechst said that its generics business experienced particular price pressures in the U.S. last year.</p>
<p>--Svea Herbst-Bayliss, Frankfurt  Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
